          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"}> general relativity
            ),
            %em higher curvature corrections
            are modifications of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            that include not just the linear appearance of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+curvature"} scalar curvature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            but higher scalar powers of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+curvature+tensor"} Riemann curvature tensor
          %p
            When viewing Einstein-Hilbert
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            valid at low
            = succeed "/long" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavelengths"} wavelengths
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            come with infinite towers of higher curvature corrections.
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inflaton+field"} inflaton field
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Starobinsky+model+of+cosmic+inflation"} Starobinsky model of cosmic inflation
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            that extremizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            for given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            and
            %em arbitrary
            higher curvature correction is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+spacetime"} universal spacetime
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#for_11d_supergravity For 11d Supergravity
          %p
            A systematic analysis of the possible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+curvature+corrections"} higher curvature corrections
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            makes the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/I8"} I8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic 8-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 48
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo −
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
